cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "STUR Resistance Equation: Derivation Record"
abstract: >-
  Resistance is one loop phase, Phi_R, whose variance is entropy, whose
  energy cost is set by temperature, and whose ceiling is set by boundary
  area. One line is a STUR postulate, S_R = 1/2 k_B Phi_R^2. The record
  documents that the postulate and its corollary failed their computed tests
  against standard decoherence theory, and that the Smarr consistency check
  was circular. What survives is a synthesis of known physics (REPORT.md).
  Every number is reproduced by the scripts in src/.
authors:
